you do something great and then you come  back and you go we've got to raise the  bar again in a major franchise like thor  there's bound to be tears some sweat and  quite a bit of overall pain it does  become like a sport and you're sweating  and you there's injuries and so on  number one natalie portman did many of  her own stunts in thor love and thunder  which meant she had to be strong she  shares a bit about her training regimen  i trained for a long time before  enduring and i was doing the whole  protein shake thing it really helped  prepare me for the level of action that  we ended up doing even her costume was  heavy she needed a great deal of upper  body strength just to wear it throughout  the scene the costume designer created a  more comfortable lightweight version for  her to wear during breaks not only was  it lighter but the cape was also  shortened because it seems wearing capes  caused a lot of problems for the actors  as they would often trip over them and  get hit in the face during important  moments number two taika waititi had his  hands full as the director and the  character korg he basically had to be in  two places at once this is taika  performing chord but sometimes he's in  the suit the like motion capture suit  whilst directing sometimes he wasn't  actually there and the actors had to  pretend he was but most of the time he  was in full director mode while playing  korg at the same time the head you know  that's all there and there was attached  to a stick and that stick was attached  to his back essentially his head was  underneath cords the costume itself was  heavy and awkward so walking around in  it for long periods of time definitely  proved to be challenging this thing here  was attached on a harness remember that  and i also had the camera thing to  record my face talk about elaborate  number three speaking of elaborate  costumes  christian bale went through his own  trials and tribulations behind the face  of gore the godbutcher when he was first  cast he assumed gore was going to be  created with cgi but then he saw the  call sheet and noticed he had to come in  4 hours earlier than everyone else his  team of makeup artists got the process  down to three and a half hours but that  wasn't his only gore-related issue then  it wasn't until a couple of weeks later  i went wait what is this you know  because i'm swallowing an awful lot of  it yeah black bile he often had a lot of  it in his mouth while filming not only  that but christian found himself pretty  incapacitated because of gore's long  nails he tells deadline it affected my  brain i was like i can't eat i've got  long nails i was trying to type i  couldn't do anything number four chris  hemsworth is no stranger to pushing his  limits but when training for both his  fourth thor movie and a biopic for hulk  hogan he pushed himself a little too  hard though it's unclear exactly how it  happened he had to go see a specialist  for his back he opened up about the  struggles he faced i found that after  lifting weights for so long and not  getting in touch with my fast twitch  fibers the snappiness that my body had  has gone  number five you'd be surprised how much  effort went into making these screaming  goats they didn't bring any real goats  on set for those guys though because  they modeled them to be the size of  clydesdale horses it wouldn't have been  useful anyway all real hair all planted  in like each hair is actually planted in  by hand they had an entire team of  makeup artists on deck for these goat  scenes they'd run in with like a  glycerin spray and  just so the tongue was like extra wet  for that kind of reference the only real  goat they had on set was devin who  played a space goat let me tell you  devin is insufferable apparently though  very cute he wasn't the easiest to work  with because he loved eating all the  props i keep trying to explain to chris  that devin's not out to get him number  six  at first glance you might think being a  stunt double is a pretty dangerous line  of work at first glance you'd be  absolutely right bobby holland hinton  has doubled for thor james bond and  captain america and although he is an  absolute professional he still receives  a fair amount of serious injuries he  shares his most poignant onset injury  during thor i snap my groin up the bone  on thor ragnarok just doing a jumping  flip kick to try and kick the hulk in  the gladiator scene the timing of my  kick and the wire pull and me really  trying to go for it i hyperextended and  snapped a bit of my abductor longus and  rectus abdominis off the bone which took  a little while to heal  number 7 the actors of this film  described their sequences as high level  child's play for the first three days of  thor love and thunder christian bale had  to act with chris hemsworth natalie  portman and tessa thompson all gagged  and silent christian had a tiny  monologue that ended up being expanded  due to taika waititi's direction to a  massive monologue you were shouting  things at me and i was coming up with  stuff and  acting i felt like a demented nun or  something he had a really hard time with  it because he thought he was doing the  worst job ever especially because no one  could respond to him it was definitely  one of his least favorite moments also  given the fact that it was his first  introduction to the cast none of that  ended up in the film so i think that  must have been the answer  it was the worst  number eight definitely more awkward  than you'd think in thor ragnarok in  every scene that mark ruffalo who plays  the hulk performed he was isolated in a  completely different part of the set  that's how he performed all his hulk  scenes throughout the franchise except  for thor love and thunder we can thank  incredible technological advancement for  that i'm basically on one set swinging  this big hammer around so that means  when chris did his fight scene with him  he was also 